          "id": "34e82d221483b6784380c9da34d56e5f0dffdf90",
          "message": "ci: Upgrade RunsOn runners to Ubuntu 26.04 and C8/M8 (#6454)\n\n## What\n\nUpgrade RunsOn Ubuntu host images to `ubuntu26-full-x64` /\n`ubuntu26-full-arm64`, including runner-image matrices. Keep SchemaBot\non Ubuntu 24 because its older parser dependency fails to compile on\nUbuntu 26; an inline comment explains this exception.\n\nMove the oldest upgrade-test starting point from v0.21.0 / pgrx 0.16.1\nto v0.22.0 / pgrx 0.17.0, whose bindgen 0.72.1 includes newer Clang\ncompatibility fixes. Run upgrade tests on Ubuntu 26, retaining coverage\nfrom the latest release as well.\n\nUpgrade x86 compute runner families from `c7a+c7i` to `c8a+c8i`,\nmatching Cloud PR #1071, and general-purpose runner families from\n`m7a+m7i` to `m8a+m8i`. ARM family pools and `c8gd.metal-24xl` benchmark\nrunners remain unchanged. Inline comments explain M-family memory\nallocations.\n\nPartition native Rust caches by build distribution/version and the pgrx\nPostgreSQL cache by runner image. This prevents restoring Ubuntu 24\nbinaries that depend on unavailable libraries such as `libicui18n.so.74`\nonto Ubuntu 26.\n\nThe change preserves runner architecture, CPU/RAM allocations, Spot\nsettings, job containers, and package target distributions.\n\nRunsOn lists both images as supported:\nhttps://runs-on.com/docs/runners/platforms/. Its image repository\ncurrently notes that Ubuntu 26 images are built on demand rather than on\nthe regular schedule:\nhttps://github.com/runs-on/runner-images-for-aws#linux.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Actionlint validation of workflows, shared-action YAML parsing, and\n`git diff --check` passed.\n- Audited native-cache consumers for distribution separation; container\npackage caches already include their target distribution.\n- CI validation of the compatibility fixes is pending.\n\n## Before merge\n\nThis PR is draft pending native source-image compatibility validation.\nBenchmarker compiles pg_search on the host and copies the shared library\ninto a released Docker image. A newer host libc/toolchain can introduce\nruntime requirements absent from that image; verify extension loading\nand queries on the resulting image before merging, or move compilation\ninto a compatible build container. The manual Cloud image workflow has\nthe same constraint where present. Containerized package builds retain\ntheir existing target distributions.",
