          "distinct": true,
          "id": "205cbc63bb5c3c065ff82c6097397a2252671eef",
          "message": "fix: adapt IVF clustering to Tantivy's vector router API (#6432)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Closes #\n\n## What\n\nPin Tantivy at `91abdcf3` (router cleanup) and adapt pg_search to that\nvector API.\n\n- `training_samples_per_centroid` becomes `training_sample_ratio`\n(default `0.32`)\n- Every index open selects `RouterKind::Rng`, Tantivy's default centroid\nrouter\n- SuperKMeans moves to 0.2.0 so the leaf count follows the sample\n\n## Why\n\nThe vector router redesign is a separate review from the later\nstreaming-merge pin. This is the bottom of the stack; #6433 moves the\npin to Tantivy tip.\n\nThis is a breaking index-option change and should ship as 0.26.0, not a\n0.25.x patch. Indexes created with `training_samples_per_centroid` will\nnot open after upgrade.\n\n## How\n\n`IvfClusterer` now reports a sample ratio and trains without a fixed\ncentroid count. `open_index` sets the RNG router, which Tantivy requires\nto build or open IVF segments.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo check -p pg_search`\n- `cargo test -p pg_search --lib vector::clusterer::tests`\n- `vector_merge` regress comments updated for primary-only assignment\n\nNix `cargoHash` is still the pre-bump value. CI should commit the\ncorrected hash onto this branch.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-bot[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
