          "distinct": true,
          "id": "16384816f48a26d866f343d4339ebe719dfa695d",
          "message": "perf: Prune posting list metadata for UUID and JSON (#6441)\n\n## What\n\nConfigure range fields, UUID fields, and keyword tokenizers (`keyword`,\n`raw`, `literal_normalized`) to store the minimum posting list metadata\n(`IndexRecordOption::Basic`, `fieldnorms = false`) and enable `fast =\ntrue` by default. Update range query construction to request\n`IndexRecordOption::Basic`.\n\n## Why\n\nThese field types and tokenizers are used for exact term matching, range\nbounds filtering, or sorting. They do not utilize BM25 term frequencies,\npositions, or field length normalization (`fieldnorms`). Storing\npositions, frequencies, and norms for them wastes index space and page\ncache.\n\n## How\n\n- In `pg_search/src/schema/config.rs`:\n- `default_uuid()`: set `record = IndexRecordOption::Basic` and\n`fieldnorms = false`.\n  - `default_range()`: return `SearchFieldConfig::Range { fast: true }`.\n- `From<SearchFieldConfig> for JsonObjectOptions` for `Range`: set\n`IndexRecordOption::Basic`, `fieldnorms: false`, and `tokenizer: \"raw\"`.\n- `text_from_json()` and `json_from_json()`: single-token tokenizers\ndefault to `fast: true`, `record: IndexRecordOption::Basic`, and\n`fieldnorms: false` when omitted in JSON options.\n- In `pg_search/src/query/range.rs`: Set `const RECORD:\nIndexRecordOption = IndexRecordOption::Basic`.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded and existing regress tests.",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-28T10:53:25-07:00",
          "tree_id": "41b239a718d594f7ee260853b1a41009377c658f",
