          "id": "29b0bfe2ad82ed71cce56fb22adc25860827ca72",
          "message": "refactor: separate a fast field's identity, shape, and delivery (#6207)\n\n# Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- Part of #6164 (step 1 of the three in the description, no behavior\nchange)\n\n## What\n\nSplit a named fast field's identity, shape, and delivery into three\nindependent axes on `WhichFastField`.\n\n## Why\n\nDelivery was baked into the variant list, so `Named` needed a `Deferred`\ntwin and arrays needed twins of their own. The shape problem is worse:\n`SearchFieldType` has no array variant and `is_array` lives on\n`CategorizedFieldData`, which never reaches this enum, so there was no\nway to say \"this column holds a list\". #6149 hit exactly that while this\nbranch was in flight and added a third twin, `Array(String,\nSearchFieldType)`, with its own hand-rolled `List(Field::new(\"item\",\n..))` and parallel arms in the scan paths.\n\n## How\n\n`FieldDelivery` and `FieldCardinality` are separate from `field_type`,\nfollowing how Arrow keeps a `Field` separate from the encoding of the\narray carrying it. `arrow_data_type` wraps in `DataType::List` with\nArrow's `\"item\"` child name when the cardinality is `List`.\n\nThe last two commits absorb #6149: `Array` becomes `Named { cardinality:\nList, delivery: Eager }`, its arms either collapse into Named patterns\nthat already match both cardinalities or become the List half of a\ncardinality dispatch with bodies kept verbatim, and `list_item_field`\ngives the four hand-built `\"item\"` fields one constructor. `find_field`\nkeeps resolving list columns to their element type, as on main. One gate\nis explicit where the variant split used to be load-bearing:\n`enable_deferred_columns` defers `Scalar` columns only, since the\ndeferred union encoding carries one value per row; on main `Array` could\nnever be flipped to deferred, and list late materialization is #6164\nitself (the TODO in `ensure_column_fetched` carries over).\n\nAlso collapses repetition the axes exposed. `WhichFastField::to_eager`\nand `PgSearchTableProvider::active_fields` replace three hand-rolled\ncopies of the same eager view, one of which arrived with #6139.\n`SearchFieldType::is_dictionary_storage` and `is_bytes_storage` replace\ntwo open-coded copies of the same four-variant Arrow match and a third\nthat spelled out its bytes-only subset.\n\nLeft alone deliberately: the `is_bytes: bool` that `DeferredField` and\nthe lookup decoders carry, and the `DeferredCtid` / `Ctid` delivery\ntwin. The first is storage propagation rather than classification and\nruns through `late_materialization.rs` and `deferred_lookup.rs`; the\nsecond needs `name` to become a universal field, which is a wider\nchange. Say if you want either folded in here.\n\nRebased onto #6219, which lands in the same two files. Its\n`fetch_ordinals_in_scan` and the new `deferred_lookup.rs` construct the\ntuple forms this PR replaces, so both are translated to the struct form;\nthe `deferred_lookup` site takes `eager()`, matching the variant it used\nbefore.\n\n## Tests\n\nBehavior neutral: 343/343 on pg18 with no expected output touched, run\non the final tree. The only test edits are mechanical constructor\nupdates where unit tests build the enum. The lateral unnest suite from\n#6149 now runs its array columns through `FieldCardinality::List`.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mohammad Dashti <mdashti@gmail.com>",
