          "id": "248a4e6ac0c3cb3fc556a6ecbd33372e0ca1668e",
          "message": "test: added static heap churn to five qgen proptests (#6377)\n\n## Ticket(s) Closed\n\n- None directly. The churn surfaced these, all fixed on `main`:\n  - #6374, fixed by #6348\n  - #6375, fixed by #6378\n  - #6376, fixed by #6380\n  - #6363, fixed by #6381\n  - #6353, fixed by #6383\n\n## What\n\nThis PR churns the qgen fixture once, right after the schema, so the\noracle runs against a heap that has seen inserts, deletes, updates and\nvacuums instead of a freshly built, all-visible one.\n\nFive `generated_*` tests get a churned `rstest` case, one per\nstate-sensitive path: base scan, join scan, aggregate over a join,\naggregate pushdown, and a subquery under parallel workers. The other\neleven keep the clean case they already had. `PARADEDB_QGEN_CHURN=off`\nmakes the churned case run clean too.\n\n## Why\n\nThe oracle compared PostgreSQL and ParadeDB on tables where every block\nwas all-visible, so the paths that defer or skip visibility work never\nsaw a row they had to filter. The clean case stays as the control: a\nfailure that shows up only in the churned case needs the mutations.\n\nThe query shape matters less than the state. Every fix this found\nreduces to a plain query. What no hand-written test had was the heap\nunderneath: a redirect line pointer on an all-visible page, an emptied\nmutable segment, a segment with no column for a JSON path.\n\n## How\n\n- The mutations come from `PARADEDB_QGEN_SEED`, the seed the fixture's\nrows already come from, and run once before any case.\n- The heap then holds still, so a failing case shrinks its query against\nthe heap it failed on and the seed persists like any other failure.\n- The churn SQL joins the fixture's script as it lands, so a failure\nprints the schema, the churn and the two queries, in the order they ran.\n- Rows another backend holds in flight are out of scope. They need a\nlive second session, which no printed script can replay, so those belong\nin stressgres.\n\n## Tests\n\nTest-only.",
