          "distinct": true,
          "id": "0e550ae6a5b5166dcbb4056c54f0d4ff1bb9b59a",
          "message": "ci: limit workflow checkout and fetch history (#6571)\n\n## What\n\nLimit Git fetches in cherry-pick, schema, query/stressgres benchmark,\nupgrade-test, and release workflows instead of downloading every branch\nand tag's full history.\n\n## Why\n\nThe cherry-pick checkout in run 36748670883 was still fetching after\nnine minutes. Other workflows also fetch full history despite only using\nspecific revisions and release tags.\n\n## How\n\n- Use depth-1 checkouts for cherry-picks, schema tests, query/stressgres\nbenchmarks, and upgrade tests. The backport action fetches required\nsource commits and target branches; schema tests already fetch their\nbase separately.\n- Fetch release tags explicitly at depth 1 for upgrade discovery and\ntests, preserving version selection, tagged file reads, prior-version\ncheckout, and SQL predecessor lookup. Limit subsequent PR-head/commit\nfetches to depth 1.\n- Use depth 2 for release checkout, release tags, and branch freshness\nchecks to retain the parent needed for artifact diffs. Fetch main\nseparately at depth 1 when syncing artifacts.\n- Keep full history in migration checks because dependency validation\ninspects commit ancestry.\n\n## Tests\n\n- All workflow and composite-action YAML parsed successfully; git diff\n--check passed.\n- Local Git fixture checks passed for shallow branch resolution,\nannotated release tags and tagged file reads, upgrade PR-ref switching,\nrelease parent diffs, and main checkout/artifact copying.\n- Verified backport-action v4 fetches source commits with required\nparents and each target branch.\n- Live checkout timing, database tests, benchmarks, and release\npublishing remain to be verified in GitHub Actions.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Philippe Noël <21990816+philippemnoel@users.noreply.github.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-30T10:36:07-07:00",
